>would an energetically very strong potential hill for the fuel to climb
>to reach the ship.  For a ship moving at relativistic speeds most of the
>energy of the fuel would be lost in the climb.  

It seems reasonable to assume a constant max energy one can stuff
through this end of the hole per time unit, and to then calculate how
the acceleration of the other end would slow down as it gets faster,
and compute a empire-time/distance table from that.  Constant
acceleration now sounds implausible. 

And there might be a max speed set by having to suffer intersellar
dust grains n cosmic radiation.  You will sound flakey if you don't
even mention these concerns.

>Brute force invasion would be suicide for the invaders and
>their whole empire: once defeated the invader's whole wormhole connected
>empire would be open to subversion from 'aliens from tomorrow'.

